From dd7f74968b9939c0be73eb1915cc23c3a90bc7fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 02:32:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(control): bound every layout request and make an
 unanswered save an explicit state (A6)

Deep-audit finding A6 on #789's stack (analytics layout editor and adapter).
A request had no deadline and no cancellation: a hung credential refresh,
header or body wait left the editor busy for ever, a late answer could land
after the owner moved on, and an unanswered save was reported as neither
saved nor failed.

- js/control-room/bounded-request.js: one helper for Control editors. Every
  await of a request (credential refresh, headers, body) sits under one
  deadline; the transport gets an AbortSignal; a generation counter drops
  whatever settles late; a newer request supersedes the older one. It never
  retries. Without timers or AbortController it refuses to construct.
- The adapter and the editor use it. Without the helper the editor stays
  unavailable instead of running unbounded.
- A save with no usable answer is the state `unknown`: the arrangement is
  kept, writes stay off, and only an explicit readback reconciles it (it says
  what was stored). A possibly committed save is never replayed.
- Tests: control-bounded-request (9), adapter (14), a browser recovery journey
  at 390 and 1280 (late success from a transport that ignores abort, hung
  stages, superseded loads, missing helper).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
