+## Bounded requests and recovery (deep-audit finding A6)
+
+`js/control-room/bounded-request.js` is the one helper the adapter and the editor
+both use. It puts every await of a request (credential refresh, response headers,
+response body) under one deadline, hands the transport an `AbortSignal`, and its
+generation counter discards whatever settles late. It never retries. The deadline
+is 15 s by default; `timeoutMs` on `CR.analyticsLayoutAdapter.create` and on
+`CR.analyticsLayout.bind` changes it. Controls are off only while a request is
+inside its deadline, so Reload always comes back.
+
+The editor publishes its state as `data-layout-state` on the editor section:
+`unavailable`, `loading`, `saving`, `ready`, `locked` (reload first) or `unknown`.
+
+- A read with no answer ends `locked`; "Reload saved layout" retries the read.
+- A save that never left the page (the sign-in check stalled or failed first)
+  changes nothing: arrangement and revision stand and Save is usable again.
+- A save that was sent and did not end in success, a conflict (409) or a denial
+  (401/403) may have committed: deadline, lost connection, unreadable body,
+  unusable envelope, service error. The editor enters `unknown`: the owner's
+  arrangement stays on screen, edits and Save stay off, and nothing is replayed.
+  "Reload saved layout" is the readback. If the stored layout matches the
+  arrangement, nothing more needs storing. If it does not, the arrangement returns
+  as unsaved changes against the freshly read revision and only the owner's next
+  Save sends it. A failed readback keeps both the arrangement and the state.
+- The kept arrangement lives in the mounted editor only. Remounting the editor or
+  reloading the page drops it and simply reads the stored layout again.
+- A conflict (409) behaves as before. Access or account loss aborts the request in
+  flight and clears the editor, arrangement included; `dispose()` aborts too.
+
+The adapter labels a failed save: `error.outcome` is `not_sent`, `unknown`, or
+absent when the service refused it with a status below 500. `load`, `save` and
+`identity` accept `{signal}`; the editor passes its own.
 
